Dear Mr Goodwin, Dr Farrar, Ms Sackman MP and Ms Davies-Jones MP,

=20

Please find attached my Stage 2 Escalation Letter (dated 29 October 2025) c=
oncerning HMCTS=E2=80=99s handling of my Pre-Action correspondence of 20 and 21 Oc=
tober 2025 and my Urgent Escalation Letter of 28 October 2025.

The matter has been misclassified as a judicial complaint rather than addre=
ssed as a Pre-Action notice alleging administrative and equality-law breache=
s under FPR Part 3A, the Equality Act 2010 and Article 6 ECHR. This has prev=
ented any substantive engagement with the procedural and accessibility failu=
res I raised, despite clear evidence of discriminatory treatment and the unl=
awful revocation of my participation measures post-trial.

=20

Given the seriousness of these issues =E2=80=94 which go to the integrity of the =
administration of justice and equal access for disabled litigants =E2=80=94 I resp=
ectfully request that this Stage 2 escalation be:

=20
Acknowledged immediately;
Reviewed at senior management level; and
A substantive response issued within seven (7) days.
=20

For transparency and institutional accountability, this correspondence has =
also been copied to the Court of Appeal and relevant oversight and equality =
advocacy bodies.

=20

Thank you for your immediate attention to this matter.

=20

Yours sincerely,

Nadia Zahmoul

Email: nadia@rosekross.com

Case No: CA-2024-001342 / BV20D01752

=20

Attachments=20

Stage 2 Escalation Letter (29 Oct 2025)

HMCTS Correspondence + Rebuttal Summary

Pre-Action Protocol Letter + Annex A (20 Oct 2025)

Follow-Up Letter (21 Oct 2025)

Urgent Escalation Letter (28 Oct 2025)

Letter to Autism Act 2009 Committee (24 Oct 2025)

=20

=20

=20

=20

=20


